# Settings pages layout

Private settings / config shells share one content width so pages do not feel narrower than General Settings.

## Page shell

Outer page: `min-h-screen bg-background` (add `text-foreground` when the page sets it elsewhere).

Inner content container:

```tsx
<div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 space-y-4">
```

- Use `max-w-7xl` — not `max-w-3xl` / `max-w-4xl` for the page shell.
- Keep `mx-auto px-4 py-8`; vertical rhythm may be `space-y-4` or `space-y-6`.
- Dialogs, tooltips, and form fields may still use their own narrower `max-w-*`.

## Header + section tabs (top right)

When a settings page has multiple sections (route tabs or mode switches), put a [`ToggleButtonBar`](client/src/components/ui/toggle-button-bar.tsx) in the **page header row, top right** — same row as back + title, not a full-width bar under the header.

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3 mb-6">
  <div className="flex items-start gap-4 min-w-0 flex-1">
    {/* back button + title + short description */}
  </div>

  <ToggleButtonBar
    className="shrink-0"
    value={activeTab}
    onValueChange={...}
    listClassName="flex"
  >
    {TABS.map(({ id, label, Icon }) => (
      <ToggleButtonBarTrigger key={id} value={id} className="gap-1.5">
        <Icon className="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        {label}
      </ToggleButtonBarTrigger>
    ))}
  </ToggleButtonBar>
</div>
```

- Left: back control, title, optional one-line description (`min-w-0 flex-1`).
- Right: `ToggleButtonBar` with `shrink-0` so it stays top-right; wrap with `flex-wrap` on narrow viewports.
- Prefer this over a second full-width tab row under the header (SEO/GEO, Security).
- Exception: General [`SettingsPage`](client/src/pages/SettingsPage.tsx) keeps a full-width `ToggleButtonBarList` under the title because it hosts many `TabsContent` panels in one page — do not use that as the default for new multi-route settings shells.
- Visual contract for the bar itself stays in [`ui-and-design.mdc`](ui-and-design.mdc) (Toggle button bars).

## Third-party integrations — Test connection

Every settings surface that wires an external API, cloud credential, or vendor SDK **must** ship a **Test connection** action. Saving YAML or env alone is not enough — staff need a one-click probe that proves credentials and reachability before they leave the page.

### Staff UI

- Label: **Test connection** (loading: **Testing…** with spinner).
- Place next to **Save** in the connection card actions row (`variant="secondary"`, prefer `IconPlugConnected`), or in the connection card header when Save lives elsewhere (Search Console property card).
- Disable when the integration is off, required fields are empty, or the user lacks edit capability.
- Success / failure via toast: short title (`Connection OK` / `Connection failed`) plus a concrete detail (dataset date, coverage state, missing role, HTTP error) — not a bare “ok”.
- `data-testid` like `button-*-test` / `button-*-test-connection`.

### Server

- Dedicated `POST /api/settings/<integration>/test` (or equivalent staff route) gated by the same capability as Save.
- Run a real, cheap probe against the vendor (list tables, inspect one URL, ping API with key) — do not only re-validate local YAML.
- Response shape: `{ ok: boolean, error?: string, ...usefulProbeFields }` with `200` when `ok`, `4xx` when the probe fails for config/auth reasons.
- Test must **not** persist settings, start long jobs, or spend significant quota when a lighter call exists. Document any unavoidable side effects in staff copy or advanced.

### Exemplars

- OpenRush — [`SearchConsoleOpenRushCard`](client/src/components/settings/SearchConsoleOpenRushCard.tsx) + `POST /api/settings/openrush/test`
- GSC BigQuery — [`SearchConsoleBigQueryCard`](client/src/components/settings/SearchConsoleBigQueryCard.tsx) + `POST /api/settings/search-console/bigquery/test`
- Search Console URL Inspection — [`SearchConsoleTab`](client/src/components/settings/SearchConsoleTab.tsx) connection card

### Education layer

- **Staff:** Always-visible copy should say that Save stores config and Test connection verifies the live vendor link (and what it does *not* do — e.g. does not request indexing). Paths and env key names go under **Read more (advanced)**.
- **Agents:** Mutating MCP tools that change third-party config should mention Test connection (or the probe endpoint) in `next_actions` when relevant.

## Applies to

- [`SettingsPage`](client/src/pages/SettingsPage.tsx) (General) — shell width; tab placement exception above
- [`SeoGeoSettingsPage`](client/src/pages/SeoGeoSettingsPage.tsx) — header + top-right tabs (canonical)
- [`AISettingsPage`](client/src/pages/AISettingsPage.tsx)
- [`SecurityPage`](client/src/pages/SecurityPage.tsx) — header + top-right tabs

Sibling admin surfaces (Tracking, Background Pipeline, Diagnostics) may use a different width when the content warrants it; do not copy their shell onto Settings pages. New third-party cards on those surfaces still follow **Test connection** above.
